**Updating video support**

I need to clarify that "![video]" is a standard image alt text but lacks semantic meaning. Our current import only processes image-only paragraphs with alt text reading "video." I think we could enhance support by using alt text in the `video: title` format. It seems like we need to adjust our HTML to utilize semantic `<video>` tags and include attributes like playbackUrl, coverUrl, and title. Additionally, thoughtful consideration for how we identify and manage these elements will be essential.
**Updating codec functionality**

I'm thinking about the plain text codec and how the existing `[video: assetId]` is losing its display. It seems like I might need to update it, perhaps by using fallback options like title, description, file, playback URL, or asset ID. I also need to remember that this is a one-way export. I'll test it out and inspect the block node JSON from the Rich Text Document to pin down the exact changes needed.
